  "notes": "Sheet 0 (Verónica Durán Arquitecto, La Providencia, Gijón): a minimalist house on rising ground facing a lawn: walls of a grey-taupe render, two storeys of rectilinear boxes, glass-balustraded terraces and floor-to-ceiling glass, a tall double-height glazed stair hall between two solid render walls (photograph 3), pale stone paving round it; downhill, a half-buried lower level whose roof is a planted garden overhanging the entrance and giving shaded parking (first photograph); inside, wood floors, white walls and a timber-treaded stair behind glass (not modelled). Modelled: the lower level and its overhanging garden slab, the two upper boxes, the glazed stair hall, terrace and balustrades, paved terraces, stepping stones, trees. Guessed: dimensions (a 18 x 12 m house), the exact stagger of the boxes, colours of the render (read as taupe-grey from the photographs). A private home placed at its town only (Gijón)."
